# Processes and supervisors

```elixir
Mix.install([{:kino, "~> 0.19"}])
```

## Message passing

This notebook spawns processes that exchange messages, starts a supervision tree, and kills one of its processes to see it restarted, while Kino draws what happens. First, three processes compute squares concurrently and send them back.

```elixir
Kino.Process.render_seq_trace(fn ->
  parent = self()
  for i <- 1..3, do: spawn(fn -> send(parent, {:square, i * i}) end)

  for _ <- 1..3 do
    receive do
      {:square, square} -> square
    end
  end
end)
```

## A supervision tree

```elixir
children = [
  {Agent, fn -> %{} end},
  Task.Supervisor,
  {DynamicSupervisor, strategy: :one_for_one}
]

{:ok, supervisor} = Supervisor.start_link(children, strategy: :one_for_one)
Kino.Process.sup_tree(supervisor)
```

## Crashing and restarting

Kill the agent: its supervisor starts a new one in its place.

```elixir
agent = fn ->
  {Agent, pid, _, _} = List.keyfind(Supervisor.which_children(supervisor), Agent, 0)
  pid
end

before = agent.()
Process.exit(before, :kill)
Process.sleep(100)

[before: before, after: agent.()]
```
